Description: Evaluates the special functions of mathematical physics and
    statistics, including gamma, beta, error, Bessel, Airy, hypergeometric,
    elliptic and zeta functions, for real and complex arguments, using the
    same kernels as the 'SciPy' library's 'scipy.special' module
    (<https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/special.html>). Functions
    keep 'SciPy' names and argument order so that code translates directly
    between 'Python' and 'R', and results agree with 'SciPy' to within its
    own test tolerances. 'SciPy' is described in Virtanen et al. (2020)
    <doi:10.1038/s41592-019-0686-2>. A registered C interface lets other
    packages call the functions from compiled code.
